Jahshaka patch 0086 - the irradiance field's cage can be DECLINED for a pixel.

MEDIA patch (`Samples/Media/Hlms/Pbs/Any/IrradianceField_piece_ps.any`). No Ogre
recompile is needed for it, but Studio stages Hlms media from the SOURCE tree
(`cmake/IncludeOgre.cmake`), so EVERY TREE MUST HAVE RUN THE PATCH LOOP -
`irisgl/scripts/build-ogre.sh` - before its media is correct. It OVERLAPS patch
0058 in this file (0058 added the five hooks inside the body; this one adds the
gate around it), so the per-patch reverse check reports the familiar overlap
false positive and a tree that carries 0058 must reset the submodule before the
loop, as the stack's other overlaps already require.

WHY A PATCH AND NOT A WORKAROUND (owner rule, 2026-09-15; ledger sections 325
and 937). GATHER-1a gives a pixel its diffuse GI from a SCREEN PROBE's rays, and
the accounting rule this renderer has held since the field landed is that a
pixel receives exactly ONE diffuse-GI term. Two halves of that rule a host can
already reach from outside: the voxel-cone diffuse is compiled out by a pass
property (`vct_disable_diffuse`, set from our Hlms listener), and the gather's
own term is added at an insertion point. The third half - the field's
eight-probe cage - is NOT reachable: patch 0058's five hooks are all INSIDE the
cage body, so a host can add to the cage, modulate its scale and append terms
after it, but cannot decline it. Subtracting the field's answer back out at the
post hook is not the same thing and is not free: by then the eight irradiance
fetches, the eight depth fetches and the Chebyshev test have been paid, and the
two estimates have already been summed in a half-float.

The alternatives were weighed and rejected. UNBINDING the field for gather
passes is a process-wide `HlmsPbs::setIrradianceField` (the sVctBindingOwner
trap) and would take it from the fallback pixels that need it in the same frame.
Gating upstream's whole `applyIrradianceField` insertion at
`800.PixelShader_piece_ps.any` behind a property is a coarser patch to a hotter
file and would take the field from every pixel of the pass, not from the pixels
a probe answered. RE-IMPLEMENTING the cage in our own piece is the copy-body
liability 0058 removed.

WHAT THE PATCH ADDS - one variable, one hook, two braces:

  1. `float ifdCageEnabled = 1.0;` and `@insertpiece( custom_ps_ifdCageGate )`,
     immediately after the prologue hook, so a host piece may set it with
     `ifdGridPos`, `ifdSpaceNormal` and whatever the prologue declared in scope.
  2. The eight-probe LOOP runs under `if( ifdCageEnabled != 0.0 )`. The body
     keeps its own indentation deliberately: the patch is three added lines
     rather than a re-indentation of fifty, and what the brace changes is
     whether the cage runs, not what it computes.
  3. The composite add runs under the same condition - with the cage declined
     `sumIfdWeight` is zero and that line would divide by it. The RESOLVE hook
     stays outside the branch, because a host declares its own quantities there
     and reads them in the post hook, which must run for every pixel: the pixels
     the field does not answer are exactly the ones a host's fallback is for.

Left at one - every build that defines no piece for the new hook, which is every
build today - the generated shader carries one constant initialisation and two
branches on a compile-time-constant expression, and the picture is unchanged.

VERIFICATION. `git apply --check` against the pin with the stack through 0058
applied, and `git apply --reverse --check` after applying. Both selftest hashes
are UNCHANGED with the hook undefined and with GATHER-1a's own piece defining it
while the gather's row is off: pose 1
777eb2f12a15811a75a0fda1e7c746acbf07a030fca69e658c3132ebc3ffa7be, pose 2
c2c2b19f6c95351fbe6163b2036256fb240054e176dff87afe0e014fdf241d74.

